t-common-dir resolver; the shared part is two lines of formatting."},{"location":"tests/router_inbox.rs:194","claim":"The orphan test and the oversized-post test pin post's private .new. temp-file naming, so a rename breaks them without any behaviour change.","why":"The .new. prefix is status's orphan rule too (scripts/router-inbox.sh:189 tied to :119; status contract orphans=<n> in erguard-w3-inbox-plan.html:117), so a rename does change count behaviour; the filter at tests/router_inbox.rs:246 feeds a negative check (:248) that would still pass, not break."},{"location":"scripts/router-inbox.sh:185","claim":"inbox/read/ grows without bound and status stats every entry on each call, so its cost grows with all past traffic.","why":"Deliberate: DEC-57 (docs/decisions/router.html:185) accepts read/ growth with cleanup a manual move; scripts/router-inbox.sh:22-23 rules out a delete verb; the plan's status contract requires read=<n> (erguard-w3-inbox-plan.html:117, scan at scripts/router-inbox.sh:184-187); the hot path watch (:135-152) never scans read/."}],"nits":[{"location":"tests/router_inbox.rs:185","finding":"an_empty_or_consumed_inbox_times_out_with_exit_1 takes about 2.17 s because it runs two watch 1 timeouts with ROUTER_INBOX_POLL=1; the second only checks a consumed message does not return, which watch 0 checks in one scan (scripts/router-inbox.sh:135-149), saving about 1 s."},{"location":"tests/router_inbox.rs:1-5","finding":"The module doc names its contract as 'the 2026-11-14 probe's 28 checks' and 'the ones the round-1 review added': the probe is git-ignored (docs/decisions/router.html:182,186), the file has 26 tests, and review history in a code comment goes stale (rubric P5)."}],"fleet":{"dimensions":["correctness","efficiency","altitude"],"finders":3,"verifiers":6,"verifier_model":"claude-opus-5-5","candidates":{"blocker":1,"important":7,"nit":11},"by_finder":{"correctness":{"found":7,"verified":7},"efficiency":{"found":5,"verified":4},"altitude":{"foun